Description: LTSP display manager (GTK3 / xfreerdp fork)
 ldm is an X11 display manager similar to xdm, gdm and kdm, used by LTSP
 (Linux Terminal Server Project) thin clients. This fork replaces the
 GTK2 greeter with a GTK3 one (required to build at all on current
 Debian releases, which no longer ship GTK2), adds an xfreerdp backend
 plugin (auto-detecting xfreerdp3/xfreerdp2, credentials passed via
 stdin instead of argv, optional default RDP domain) alongside the
 original ssh backend, and carries a number of security and
 correctness fixes found during an internal audit (argv-based process
 spawning instead of shell word-splitting, a heap buffer overflow fix
 in the LTSP-Cluster load-balancer client, path-traversal and
 NULL-pointer-dereference fixes, and standard hardening compiler
 flags).

